# {{project_name}}

An NFT Marketplace smart contract for Stellar/Soroban, generated by
[soroban-forge](https://github.com/soroban-forge-labs/soroban-forge) from the
`nft-marketplace` template.

## How it works

The marketplace facilitates trustless, escrowed sales of NFTs conforming to
the Soroban NFT template interface:

1. **Deployment & Config** — The marketplace is deployed with an `admin`, a
   `treasury` address, and a `fee_bps` protocol fee (in basis points, where
   100 bps = 1%). The fee is capped at `MAX_FEE_BPS` = 1000 (10%); the
   constructor and `set_fee_bps` reject anything higher with `InvalidFee`. The
   admin can update treasury and fee settings as needed.
2. **Listing an NFT** — A seller calls `list(seller, nft_contract, token_id, payment_token, price)`.
   The NFT is transferred from the seller to the marketplace contract for escrow,
   and the protocol fee in force at that moment is stored in the listing.
3. **Buying an NFT** — A buyer calls `buy(buyer, nft_contract, token_id)`. The
   purchase price is split into the treasury fee and seller payout using the
   fee stored in the listing, transferred atomically, and the escrowed NFT is
   transferred to the buyer.
4. **Cancelling a Listing** — The seller can call `cancel(seller, nft_contract, token_id)`
   at any time prior to purchase to cancel the listing and reclaim their escrowed NFT.

## Fee rules

- **The fee is fixed per listing.** `list` records the current `fee_bps` in the
  `Listing`, and `buy` uses that recorded value. If the admin calls
  `set_fee_bps` afterwards, only listings created from then on use the new
  fee. A seller always receives the payout they agreed to when listing, and
  the admin cannot raise the fee on existing listings or front-run a purchase.
- **The fee is capped at 10%.** `MAX_FEE_BPS` is 1000 bps. Fee maths divides by
  `BPS_DENOMINATOR` (10000), so the cap can be changed without changing the
  arithmetic. If you raise the cap, make sure your users accept the higher
  ceiling.
- **The treasury address is not snapshotted.** Fees go to whatever treasury is
  set when `buy` runs.

## Commands

```sh
# Run unit tests
cargo test

# Build the release WASM file
stellar contract build

# Deploy to Testnet
stellar contract deploy \
  --wasm target/wasm32v1-none/release/{{crate_name}}.wasm \
  --source <your-identity> \
  --network testnet
```

